<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Gmzap</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>gmzap &lt;npc or object&gt; &lt;dil@zone&gt;      (230)
gmzap &lt;sym@zone&gt; &lt;dil@zone&gt;
</pre>
<p>Removes a DIL program from an NPC or object of an event: one tagged with 
<a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Gmmem</a> &lt;unit&gt; event &lt;id&gt;, as a game master tags the units it 
loads. Use it on a character that must stay put, to take off the DIL 
that makes it wander. <b>wstat &lt;unit&gt; functions</b> lists a unit's DILs by 
name; when a DIL is on a unit more than once, every copy comes off.
</p><p>It never touches rooms, treasure, players or what is theirs: what they 
carry or wear, their pets and followers. The tag marks the units of 
events but doesn't prove who loaded them, so tag only your own. To 
remove a DIL from any unit, a higher god uses <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Zap</a> (245).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Gmmem</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Zap</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Wizhelp Wstat</a>
</pre>




</div>